course: dictionary
lesson: 15842
title: Undiscovered
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Undiscovered means not yet found or known about by anyone. Break the word into parts: un- means not, and discovered means found out. So undiscovered is "not yet found out". «Scientists think there are many undiscovered species in the deep sea.» Nobody has found those creatures yet, so they are still hidden.
explain: The word can also describe people. «Maya paints beautifully, but she is still an undiscovered talent.» Nobody famous has noticed her yet. Look for context clues such as deep sea, hidden, secret or treasure. They tell you that something exists but has not been found.
explain: Try the swap check from the last lesson. Put "not yet found" in place of undiscovered: «There are many species not yet found in the deep sea» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Undiscovered means not yet found or known about by anyone.
fact: «Undiscovered» can also mean not yet famous or noticed, as in «an undiscovered talent».
fact: The prefix un- means not, so undiscovered is built from «not» and «discovered».
fact: Useful phrases: «undiscovered species», «remain undiscovered», «an undiscovered talent».
fact: Stories use undiscovered treasure, islands and secrets to make readers want to find out what happens next.
exercise: Scientists believe there are many «undiscovered species» in the rainforest. What does undiscovered mean here? | Very old and famous | Lost and sad | Cleaned and sorted | *Not yet found or known about
exercise: «The pirate's gold will remain undiscovered for a hundred years.» What does remain undiscovered mean? | Is given to the king | Is sold at the market | *Stays hidden and not found | Is shiny and new
exercise: «Priya is an undiscovered talent, and nobody has seen her paint yet.» Find and copy the word that means not yet famous or noticed. | *undiscovered | talent | yet | paint
test: «The explorers hoped to find an undiscovered island.» What does undiscovered mean? | Very small and sandy | Full of noise and people | Once owned by a king | *Not yet found by anyone
test: Which words in «Deep in the ocean lie secrets that no one has ever seen» tell you the secrets are still hidden? | lie | secrets | Deep in the ocean | *no one has ever seen
exam: Ben says undiscovered means famous. Why is he wrong, using the phrase «an undiscovered talent»? | *Undiscovered means not yet noticed, so it is the opposite of famous | Undiscovered means very famous and well known | Undiscovered means the same as talent | Undiscovered means lost at sea
